ho've made this these  accusations so the police have already  just been clear are you suggesting that  it's the media's fault that he's that  he's in the position he's in no i'm  suggesting that they started the story  for the reinvestigation the police are  then duty-bound  to open an investigation to reassess  this they're doing that through the  processes and uh kirsten has been pretty  clear he doesn't think he's broken any  rules and if he has he will do the  decent thing and he will step down and  that's not just because he's leader of  the opposition and believes in her  integrity in our politics but because he  has been a former director of public  prosecution and it didn't help that  labour lied about whether the deputy was  there or not well i don't think it was a  a lie i mean lies doing an awful lot of  heavy lifting there this was an event  that was happening  in durham there was a schedule of  attendees and there was a schedule of  what was to happen  there and everyone's pretty clear that  no rules were broken and  but we were told that she wasn't there  and she fundamentally was there well  to categorize that as a lie though is  well  a mistake and people weren't sure what  who was there i mean it's all the shape  it's all come out  now and people have said well  the investigation will now happen these  sheets that you talk about incidentally  are no smoking gun every single visit  from any shadow cabinet member have a  shared job  they must have looked at that and and  then made a decision to say that she  wasn't that way fundamentally yeah on  those sheets that also said quite  clearly what the covert rules were and  compliance with those covert rules  that's pretty clear because it's in the  public domain which shows that this was  a pre-planned uh work event the stopping  for food was part of that pre-planned  work event and the cover drills were  part of that  schedule and that's why i think that the  police will come back and say that  there's no case to answer and kirsten  was quite confident about that but he  has said and i think it's right for him  to say this that if he does get a fixed  penalty notice like the prime minister  did he will stand down because he  believes in integrity and public life  why do the good people of glasgow not  want to have jubilee celebrations do you  think  no parties at all well i don't know and  it's great in my own constituency  there's roads closed everywhere over the  weekend for people to have street  parties and come together it's yes it's  the jubilee but it's also a great  opportunity for after two years of  covert and lockdown for people to  celebrate with their neighbors to come  together to socialize to bring their  children together i think it's a great  thing for the country to do people can  make their own decisions if they want to  celebrate the jubilee but isn't it just  a great excuse to get people back  together again after the last two years  would you celebrate a ukraine victory  over scotland tonight well that's a very  difficult question probably not i mean i  wouldn't be as disappointed ordinarily  in a scotland defeat perhaps tonight and  but i do want scotland to win but i  think it will be a wonderful occasion i  hope the occasion is marked across the  world for what it is and sends a very  strong message to what putin is doing in  ukraine but i won't be as disappointed  as i would perhaps normally be but i do  want scotland to win this okay good to  talk to you thanks so much for joining  us thank you

